# Auto detect text files and perform LF normalization
* text=auto

# Force LF on checkout regardless of the checking-out machine's core.autocrlf
# setting - "text=auto" alone still lets a Windows checkout with
# core.autocrlf=true produce CRLF working-tree files. That's silently fatal
# here: Unraid's own webGui parses every plugin ".page" file by splitting on
# the LITERAL byte sequence "\n---\n" (see webGui/include/PageBuilder.php's
# build_pages()) - a CRLF-terminated "---" line means that split never
# matches, the whole file gets fed to parse_ini_string() as if it were the
# header, that fails, and the page is silently dropped from the nav/Settings
# menu with only a log line (no visible error) - exactly the "the whole
# plugin disappeared after updating" bug this fixes. Shell scripts are
# equally fatal with CRLF (a CRLF-terminated "#!/bin/bash" shebang is a
# "bad interpreter" error). package.sh copies source/stacksUI/ verbatim into
# the shipped .txz, so whatever line endings are on disk at package time are
# exactly what ships - this must be forced, not just "auto".
*.page eol=lf
*.php  eol=lf
*.js   eol=lf
*.css  eol=lf
*.sh   eol=lf
*.plg  eol=lf
source/stacksUI/event/docker_started/* eol=lf
